{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and the Cooking Accident", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Dinner Invitation", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Present Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use an active structure when you want the 'doer' of the action to be the subject.<br/> You use a passive structure when you want the 'receiver' of the action to be the subject. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\">Cab drivers</span> (subject)<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">whisk</span> people</span> (object) <span class=\"italic\">away in cabs.</span><br/>  Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\">They</span> (subject) <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">are whisked away</span> by cab!</span> (by people) <br/> <br/>It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. <br/><br/>   You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the verb followed by the past participle. <br/><br/>  The Simple Present passive form is:<br/>  am/are/is + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">English <span class=\"strong\">is spoken</span> in the United States.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "So much wine is guzzled by patrons on some nights! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am glad they are whisked away by cab! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Those who are ushered to late movies must find it hard to concentrate!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The ones who are escorted to night clubs are better off. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Alcohol is burned off quite quickly on the dance floor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The invitations to our Spicy Rice Night are sent. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The costumes and decorations that are chosen will make it quite a spectacle!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking for Clarification", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You ask for clarification when you want more details on what the other person is talking about. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You ask for clarification when it is not clear what the other person is referring to. You ask the other person to be more specific by giving you more information. <br/><br/>  You can use a question at the beginning of a statement or question to ask for clarification like: <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think it sounds a bit too intense?</span><br/><br/>  Questions within sentences are called embedded questions. Example: <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Simple question</span>: <span class=\"italic\">What are you going to do after dinner?</span><br/> <span class=\"strong\">Embedded question</span>: <span class=\"italic\">Do you know what you're going to do after dinner?</span><br/><br/>  Look at the chart below for an explanation on how to make embedded questions.<br/><br/>  You can also use a direct question.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">Is that a hint?</span><br/><br/>  Direct questions go straight to the point. Sometimes they are used to be light-hearted or to be funny.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I'm really hungry now!</span><br/> <span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: <span class=\"italic\">You mean there are times when you're not?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Embedded Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you know ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"what/where/when/who/ ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you remember ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"what/where/when/who/ ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"what/where/when/who/ ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"what/where/when/who/ ... ?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Do you know what it was called?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Can you tell me where to find it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you recall what the name of the street was? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Can you call me and tell me what day that is?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "thank goodness", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be pleased and happy about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Work is finished for the day, thank goodness.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about a big event.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to guzzle", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to drink something rapidly and eagerly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To be honest, so much wine is guzzled by patrons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to whisk", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move something or someone out of the way rapidly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The firemen whisked the students away to a safe place. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to usher", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to lead a person, group, or something to a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Those who are ushered to late movies must find it hard to concentrate!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to escort", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to accompany or lead someone or something away from some place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To my mind, the ones who are escorted to night clubs are better off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to recall", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to remember something or someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you recall what the name of the street was?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "extravaganza", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a fancy and opulent show or event", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'd love to pick up some spices for the extravaganza.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Read  Vanessa's e-mail to Sally again.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Send a friend an e-mail talking about your day or week at work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask them questions about a place they told you about.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Suggest that you go somewhere together sometime soon.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your e-mail aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write an e-mail to a frie